    "body": "Depends on: #64 (chain-telescoped redesign must land first). The A-only ablation during the 0.3% incident suggested predicted-cloud ΔT emissions contribute little to scoring quality, but the measurement was taken under the broken formula. Re-run the ablation under the fixed scorer: Gate C with F emissions enabled vs zeroed, same everything else. Acceptance: a recorded decision (keep/bound/drop ΔT) with the 4-way table showing the delta; if kept, a documented per-edge weight calibration check (top transitions sampled and eyeball-verified against corpus counts).\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- The ablation is run under the fixed (#64) scorer: Gate C with F emissions enabled vs zeroed, all else identical.\n- A written decision (keep / bound / drop ΔT) is recorded in this thread with the supporting table, and the scorer config reflects it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The comparison includes top-1 agreement and bits/token for both variants on the fixture held-out set.\n- [ ] The decision is justified by the numbers, not assertion (drop/bound requires the data to show ΔT contributes no meaningful gain).\n- [ ] If kept: a calibration spot-check of the top transition edges against corpus counts is included.",
